---
// Figure: versioned cache writes: two writers out of order, the version check,
// its weakness under eviction, and a tombstone closing the slow-reader race.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="inv-version" title="Version checks on cache writes" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. In the first three options each writer updates the cached copy after committing (write-through); in the fourth the writer invalidates with a tombstone and a reader fills. The version is a number the database increments with every change to the row. Every option was run on Redis 8.10 with the script shown in the text, using DEL in place of eviction.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="check" label="Cache writes" value="plain"
    options={[{ value: 'plain', label: 'plain SET' }, { value: 'newer', label: 'if newer' }, { value: 'evicted', label: 'if newer, evicted' }, { value: 'tombstone', label: 'if newer, tombstone' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Plain SET: writer 1 commits £37 (version 8) and stalls; writer 2 commits £35 (version 9) and sets £35 in Redis; writer 1 then sets £37. Redis serves £37 while the database holds £35, until the key expires or another write replaces it.</p>
    <p>If newer: the same order, but writer 1's late write carries version 8, and the check finds version 9 already cached, so nothing changes. Redis keeps £35.</p>
    <p>If newer, evicted: Redis evicts the key after writer 2's write. The record of version 9 goes with it, so writer 1's version 8 is compared with nothing and accepted. Redis serves £37 again until the key expires.</p>
    <p>If newer, tombstone: a slow reader reads £39 at version 7 and stalls. The writer commits £35 at version 8 and, instead of deleting the key, stores a tombstone holding version 8 and no value. The reader's late version-7 fill is refused because Redis knows version 8 exists. The next reader treats the tombstone as a miss, reads £35 at version 8, and its fill of the same version replaces the tombstone.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { switchSequence } from './switch-sequence.mjs';
  import { versionSpecs } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="inv-version"]').forEach(root => switchSequence(root, versionSpecs, 'check'));
</script>
